  "llm_analysis": {
    "quality_summary": "The dataset contains three tables (stores, sales_data, products) with generally good completeness: all columns in stores and products are fully populated. In sales_data, transaction_id has 4.3% missing values and store_id has 2.69% missing. The quantity column includes negative values, indicating returns or data entry errors, and total_amount also contains negative amounts that do not always align with quantity * unit_price (e.g., a quantity of -1 with a positive unit_price yields a negative total_amount, but some rows have mismatched signs). Customer_segment values show inconsistent abbreviations (e.g., 'Prem', 'Bgt'). Transaction_date formats are mixed (MM/DD/YYYY and ISO YYYY-MM-DD). Overall, the data is usable after cleaning and standardization.",
    "critical_issues": [
      "Missing transaction_id values (4.3% null) impede unique transaction tracking.",
